          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Ravi said, “I saw a crescent Moon, and it was rising in the East, when the Sun was setting.” Kaushalya said, “Once I saw the gibbous Moon during the afternoon in the East.” Who out of the two is telling the truth?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.268,
            0.164,
            0.884,
            0.222
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Scientific studies show that the Moon is getting farther away from the Earth and slower in its revolution. Will luni-solar calendars need an intercalary month more often or less often?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.226,
            0.883,
            0.285
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. A total of 37 full Moons happen during 3 years in a solar calendar. Show that at least two of the 37 full moons must happen during the same month of the solar calendar."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.267,
            0.289,
            0.883,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. On a particular night, Vaishali saw the Moon in the sky from sunset to sunrise. What phase of the Moon would she have noticed?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.352,
            0.883,
            0.392
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. If we stopped having leap years, in approximately how many years would the Indian Independence day happen in winter?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.396,
            0.813,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "11. What is the purpose of launching artificial satellites?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.257,
            0.422,
            0.883,
            0.463
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "12. On which periodic phenomenon are the following measures of time based: (i) day (ii) month (iii) year?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
