          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z The Moon’s crescent always faces towards the Sun (Fig. 11.12). On days when you see the crescent Moon, point your finger towards the Sun, and slowly move it across the sky towards the Moon taking as short a path as you can. Note how your finger always crosses the illuminated part of the Moon first and clearly shows us that we see sunlight reflected off the Moon. The line joining the tips of the crescent would correspond to the diameter of the Moon."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
